"The sections reinforce one another. The candlestick chart shows where price has actually traded and how far it has drifted from the open. The key levels turn that drift into R1, R2, S1 and S2 levels you can plan around. VIX tells you whether the market is priced for calm or for a shock. And the options box summarises where the big money sits: heavy open interest and the max-pain strike offer a view of what the expiry might 'want' to do. Reading the chart, levels and options together is more informative than any single number.",
